Experimental source-owned marketplace exclusion; not automatically applied by Context Foundry.
Target: can1357/oh-my-pi @ 24439066040e006eb08da7b204f0ac41c79d2de9
Owner: 003 T006 bounded-pilot-v2 startup observation and admission.
Requires prior caller/auth/refusal/restricted/catalog/settings/empty-auth/presence/telemetry patches.
Modules: marketplace-auto-update::{ownStartupMarketplace,scheduleMarketplaceAutoUpdate,retireStartupMarketplace}; main CLI explicit flag; sdk exact-session binding; CLI args/flag table.
Tests: startup-marketplace-owner.test.ts and existing SDK, main/CLI, telemetry and presence suites.
Difference: --startup-no-marketplace requires --restrict-tools. It rejects enabled,
repeated and mutable or accessor options before the original scheduler; the original
synchronous off branch completes and its exact owner retires after telemetry. Ordinary
marketplace behavior remains available without the flag. Other update routes, complete
startup inventory, Ready, paid execution, signing and release acceptance remain open.

